{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"112","question_sha256":"530070ec2a146eb095d0163efe01debf83a2c9c8765daf41e8e256210768abfe","reason":"John plays 20 × 0.80 = 16 games and receives 5 × 2 = 10 attempts per game, for 160 attempts. He makes 70% of them: 160 × 0.70 = 112.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-975"},{"independent_answer":"570","question_sha256":"8167626c4c2aab70e31e934fa565d5d086198c745d092fa6c33af085da48af5c","reason":"The school buys 2 + 2×2 = 6 models. A 5% reduction makes each $100 model cost $95, so 6 × 95 = 570.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1953"},{"independent_answer":"180","question_sha256":"ab215feab94e1c288cfd2b2ae992b5382075066908ef7a73111c1a1d45b395eb","reason":"Wednesday is 50% less than Tuesday: 50 × 0.50 = 25 km. Thursday is 40 + 25 = 65 km. Total: 40 + 50 + 25 + 65 = 180.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1895"},{"independent_answer":"1000 or 1001","question_sha256":"620deb4962d2d652017fb2a5cfedaebfb898ed1034bd4e2f80de2aa103cd60a3","reason":"The 20% margin is 2000 L × 0.20 = 400 L = 400,000 ml, equal to 1000 losses of 400 ml. After 1000 jumps the pool is exactly 80% full, while the 1001st makes it below 80%. Thus 1000 is the number of safe completed jumps, but 1001 can be read as the jump that triggers cleaning.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3557"},{"independent_answer":"345","question_sha256":"1a41c67cfa37ab5932e8605acc5068d2d25276751ad345b879c475f2fef6a9f5","reason":"Tax and tithe are each 500 × 0.10 = 50. Total deductions are 50 + 55 + 50 = 155, leaving 500 − 155 = 345.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-801"},{"independent_answer":"38","question_sha256":"70d9128e3eeeed2e881781564ec5854b6b12e4fd8c7ea4d8ccef9205762f681a","reason":"The undiscounted meal is 8 + 20 + 2×3 + 6 = 40, so the tip is 40 × 0.20 = 8. Half off the $20 entrée reduces the charged meal to $30; adding the tip gives 38.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5691"},{"independent_answer":"Underdetermined","question_sha256":"4b4badd2334c21d6585ba9e650b8f66849ba93daeed643336ffc3583463846f9","reason":"The drop is (32−8)/3 = 8 intervals, but the initial skidding probability at 32 degrees is unstated, and “increase 5%” could mean percentage points or a relative increase. The gold 24 follows only by assuming a zero baseline and eight additive 5-point increases: 40% × 60% = 24%.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-515"},{"independent_answer":"1800","question_sha256":"2c0c231c7df238746296e34bd9eb471a321ad323cc7bee69f2bef02fe1575b7d","reason":"The saving is 5 × 0.80 = 4 gallons per flush. Across 15 flushes per day and 30 days in June, the saving is 4 × 15 × 30 = 1800 gallons.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3272"}],"reviews":[{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["20 \\times 0.80 = 16 \\text{ games}","The number of free throws John gets is the total number of attempts"],"first_person":false,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":false,"key":"gsm8k-train-975:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":false,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The prefix supports calculating 160 attempts and then applying the stated 70% hit rate. It does not support equating attempts with the requested made free throws while discarding that rate.","raw_call_sha256":"193c5e30b2971e8b8bc98ef14f5dd3b4d67f2e38cb3328649733310525d289fc","reason":"The impersonal response correctly computes 16 games and 160 attempts, but incorrectly reports attempts as the answer and never applies the 70% success rate; the supported result is 112.","reusable_content":true,"status":"FAIL","student_prefix_sha256":"8254fb3f14a3b807f408bba7f1dba99f1dbcd65755fc54ead4450810f5c4cbe6","target_sha256":"5499d398d05400ba4ed6c90e7a089a5b3fe54f41425f5954f4cab1d5eb03a226"},{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["Total models bought = 2 + 4 = 6 models.","Total cost with discount = $600 - $30 = $570."],"first_person":false,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-1953:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":